ern the project. It's like a project charter or architecture decision record set. Examples:\n- \"We use functional programming where possible\"\n- \"All services must be stateless\"\n- \"No framework lock-in\"\n- \"Open source first\"\n\nThe Constitution phase defines the governing rules. Then Spec translates requirements into a specification document. Plan breaks it into work packages. Tasks are individual units. Implementation writes code. Validation runs tests.\n\nLet me present the feasibility analysis now. I'll organize it into clear sections.\n\nActually, wait — I'm also supposed to maintain a plan as files. Since I'm in plan mode and can't write files, I should present the analysis in my response and note that when we move to implementation mode, I'll create the plan file.\n\nLet me present the feasibility analysis and ask which direction the user wants to go for the Constitution phase.",
