fecycle policy\"}\n    But GET /documents/{id} still returns the document with parsed_data intact\n```\n\n**Configurable thresholds (env vars):**\n- `STORAGE_HIGH_WATERMARK_PCT` (default 85%)\n- `STORAGE_CRITICAL_PCT` (default 95%)\n- `STORAGE_ALERT_ACK_WINDOW_HOURS` (default 72)\n- `STORAGE_CRITICAL_WINDOW_HOURS` (default 24)\n- `STORAGE_LIFECYCLE_RUN_INTERVAL_MINUTES` (default 360)\n\n---\n\n### Updated API Contract\n\n```\nPOST   /api/v1/documents          → 202 {document_id, status}\n  Header: X-API-Key: <key>\n  Body (multipart/form-data):\n    file: binary (image/jpeg, image/png, image/heic, application/pdf, max 10MB)\n    type: \"invoice\" | \"ticket\" | \"payment_receipt\"\n    region: \"AR\" | ... (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2)\n  Rate limit: 60 req/min per key\n\nGET    /api/v1/documents/{id}      → 200 {document with parsed_data, validation_result}\n  Header: X-API-Key: <key>\n\nGET    /api/v1/documents           → 200 {items[], total, page, pages}\n  Header: X-API-Key: <key>\n  Query: ?status=&type=&region=&page=1&size=20\n\nGET    /api/v1/documents/{id}/image → 200 (image) | 410 (expired)\n  Header: X-API-Key: <key>\n\nGET    /api/v1/health              → 200 {status, ocr_engine, storage_pct}\n  No auth required\n```\n\n---\n\n### Updated Domain Model Additions\n\n```python\nclass DocumentStatus(str, Enum):\n    PENDING = \"PENDING\"\n    OCR_IN_PROGRESS = \"OCR_IN_PROGRESS\"\n    VALIDATING = \"VALIDATING\"\n    COMPLETED = \"COMPLETED\"\n    VALIDATION_FAILED = \"VALIDATION_FAILED\"\n    OCR_FAILED = \"OCR_FAILED\"\n    IMAGE_EXPIRED = \"IMAGE_EXPIRED\"       # NEW\n\nclass MediaType(str, Enum):              # NEW\n    JPEG = \"image/jpeg\"\n    PNG = \"image/png\"\n    HEIC = \"image/heic\"\n    PDF = \"application/pdf\"\n\nclass ApiKey(str):                       # NEW (value object, DB-stored as SHA-256)\n    prefix: str  # first 8 chars for display (e.g., \"sk-proj-...\")\n    hash: str    # SHA-256 of full key\n    created_at: datetime\n    revoked: bool\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary — All 9 Features\n\n| # | Feature | Gherkin Scenarios |\n|---|---|---|\n| F1 | Document Ingestion | 5 (JPEG, HEIC, PDF, unsupported type, oversize) |\n| F2 | Document Status Retrieval | 3 |\n| F3 | List Documents | 2 |\n| F4 | OCR Processing | 3 |\n| F5 | Regional Validation — AR | 3 |\n| F6 | Pluggable Regional Validation | 3 |\n| F7 | Rate Limiting | 4 |\n| F8 | Authentication | 4 |\n| F9 | Storage Lifecycle | 4 |\n\n---\n\n### Final Check Before Spec Approval\n\n1. **Rate limit scope:** Is 60 POST/min per key the right number for launch, or do you want it more aggressive (30/min) or looser (120/min)? Default to 60, configurable.\n\n2. **API key management:** Admin CLI only (no API self-service) — or would you want a `/keys` endpoint for operators?\n\n3. **HEIC conversion:** HEIC needs a transcoding step before OCR. Python can handle it via `pillow-heif` or `pyheif`. Should we specify that pre-processing step in the Spec, or leave it to the Plan phase?\n\n4. **PDF multi-page:** When a PDF has multiple pages, do we OCR all pages and merge, or only the first page?\n\nOtherwise — the Spec is feature-complete. Ready for your review and approval to proceed to **Plan** (where we break this into architectural decisions, component trees, task breakdown, and project scaffold).",
