          "text": "The user has approved the Spec and wants to proceed to the Plan phase. I'm in Plan mode, so I can only think, read, search, and delegate — no file modifications.\n\nThe Plan phase should produce:\n\n1. Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)\n2. Directory/package structure\n3. Component breakdown\n4. Data model (DB schema, migrations)\n5. Task breakdown (ordered, atomic, testable)\n6. pyproject.toml scaffold design\n\nLet me think through each of these systematically.\n\n### 1. Architecture Decisions\n\nKey decisions to record:\n\n1. **ADR-001: Hexagonal Architecture with Ports & Adapters**\n   - Context: We need the domain to be independent of infrastructure, testable, and swappable.\n   - Decision: Use hexagonal architecture. Domain core has no infrastructure imports. Adapters implement ports.\n   - Consequences: More boilerplate (ports/adapters) but extreme testability and flexibility.\n\n2. **ADR-002: PostgreSQL SKIP LOCKED for Job Queue**\n   - Context: We need async processing of OCR jobs. Options: Redis, RabbitMQ, or DB-backed queue.\n   - Decision: PostgreSQL SKIP LOCKED pattern. No extra infrastructure.\n   - Consequences: Simpler ops. Less scalable than Redis at high volume. Can migrate later if needed.\n\n3. **ADR-003: PaddleOCR as Primary Engine**\n   - Context: OCR engine selection. Open source, Spanish support needed.\n   - Decision: PaddleOCR primary, EasyOCR as fallback. Abstracted behind OCRPort.\n   - Consequences: Python-only, but we're Python anyway. Slightly heavier install but better accuracy.\n\n4. **ADR-004: Pydantic as Cross-Boundary Data Contract**\n   - Context: How to pass data between layers/modules.\n   - Decision: All cross-boundary data passes as Pydantic models. No raw dicts.\n   - Consequences: Strong typing, validation at edges, self-documenting.\n\n5. **ADR-005: Plugin-Based Regional Validation**\n   - Context: Regional rules must be pluggable without core changes.\n   - Decision: Validators discovered via entry points/import hooks. RegionValidator port (ABC). Validators register with their region code.\n   - Consequences: New regions = new package, no core changes. Discovery at startup.\n\n6. **ADR-006: SHA-256 API Key Storage**\n   - Context: How to store API keys securely.\n   - Decision: Keys stored as SHA-256 hashes. Prefix stored for display. Clear text shown once.\n   - Consequences: Keys can't be recovered — only rotated. Standard security practice.\n\n7. **ADR-007: Storage Lifecycle as Scheduled Job**\n   - Context: Auto-deletion of old images when storage pressure is high.\n   - Decision: Background scheduled job (APScheduler or cron-like) checks storage usage and deletes old images based on configurable thresholds.\n   - Consequences: Self-contained, no external scheduler needed.\n\n### 2. Directory/Package Structure\n\n```\ndoc-processing-service/\n├── docs/\n│   ├── constitution.md\n│   ├── spec.md\n│   ├── glossary.md\n│   └── adr/\n│       ├── 001-hexagonal-architecture.md\n│       ├── 002-postgresql-queue.md\n│       ├── 003-paddleocr-engine.md\n│       ├── 004-pydantic-boundaries.md\n│       ├── 005-plugin-regional-validation.md\n│       ├── 006-api-key-storage.md\n│       └── 007-storage-lifecycle.md\n├── src/\n│   ├── domain/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── models.py          # Pydantic models (Document, ParsedData, etc.)\n│   │   ├── enums.py           # DocumentType, DocumentStatus, MediaType\n│   │   ├── ports.py           # ABCs: OCRPort, DocumentRepositoryPort, StoragePort, RegionValidatorPort\n│   │   ├── pipeline.py        # Pipe & Filter pipeline orchestration\n│   │   └── value_objects.py   # Money, CUIT, etc.\n│   ├── services/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── document_service.py     # Application service: ingestion, status, listing\n│   │   ├── ocr_service.py          # OCR pipeline orchestration (uses OCRPort)\n│   │   ├── validation_service.py   # Regional validation orchestration (uses RegionValidatorPort)\n│   │   └── storage_lifecycle.py    # Storage lifecycle policy\n│   ├── adapters/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── rest/\n│   │   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   │   ├── api.py              # FastAPI app, route registration\n│   │   │   ├── routes/\n│   │   │   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   │   │   ├── documents.py    # /documents endpoints\n│   │   │   │   └── health.py       # /health endpoint\n│   │   │   ├── dependencies.py     # Depends() wiring (auth, rate limit, services)\n│   │   │   ├── middleware.py       # Rate limit, auth middleware\n│   │   │   └── schemas.py          # Request/Response Pydantic schemas\n│   │   ├── ocr/\n│   │   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   │   ├── paddle_ocr.py       # PaddleOCR adapter\n│   │   │   ├── easy_ocr.py         # EasyOCR fallback adapter\n│   │   │   └── preprocessor.py     # HEIC transcode, PDF rasterize, image preprocessing\n│   │   ├── repository/\n│   │   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   │   ├── postgresql.py       # PostgreSQL implementation of DocumentRepositoryPort\n│   │   │   └── migrations/         # Alembic migrations\n│   │   ├── storage/\n│   │   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   │   └── minio.py            # MinIO implementation of StoragePort\n│   │   └── validators/\n│   │       ├── __init__.py\n│   │       ├── registry.py         # Validator discovery & registry\n│   │       ├── base.py             # RegionValidator ABC\n│   │       ├── ar/                 # Argentina validators\n│   │       │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │       │   ├── invoice.py\n│   │       │   ├── ticket.py\n│   │       │   └── payment.py\n│   │       └── noop.py             # Fallback for unknown regions\n│   ├── infrastructure/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── config.py               # pydantic-settings (env vars)\n│   │   ├── database.py             # SQLAlchemy async engine, session factory\n│   │   ├── queue.py                # PostgreSQL SKIP LOCKED job queue\n│   │   ├── scheduler.py            # Storage lifecycle scheduler\n│   │   └── logging.py              # Structured logging setup\n│   ├── cli/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   └── admin.py                # API key management CLI\n│   └── main.py                     # Application entry point (uvicorn)\n├── tests/\n│   ├── bdd/\n│   │   ├── features/\n│   │   │   ├── ingestion.feature\n│   │   │   ├── status.feature\n│   │   │   ├── list.feature\n│   │   │   ├── ocr.feature\n│   │   │   ├── validation_ar.feature\n│   │   │   ├── pluggable_validation.feature\n│   │   │   ├── rate_limit.feature\n│   │   │   ├── auth.feature\n│   │   │   └── storage_lifecycle.feature\n│   │   └── steps/\n│   │       └── ...\n│   ├── unit/\n│   │   ├── domain/\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   └── adapters/\n│   └── integration/\n│       └── ...\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── Dockerfile\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── alembic.ini\n└── README.md\n```\n\n### 3. Component Breakdown\n\n**Domain Layer (core, no dependencies):**\n- `models.py` — Pydantic v2 models defining all domain entities and value objects\n- `enums.py` — All enumerations\n- `ports.py` — Abstract base classes (interfaces) for all adapters\n- `pipeline.py` — Pipe & Filter implementation: ingest filter → preprocess filter → OCR filter → parse filter → validate filter → persist filter\n- `value_objects.py` — Money, CUIT, ApiKey hash, etc.\n\n**Service Layer (orchestration, depends on ports):**\n- `document_service.py` — Ingestion orchestration (save to storage + enqueue job + return 202)\n- `ocr_service.py` — OCR pipeline execution (called by worker): preprocess → OCR → parse\n- `validation_service.py` — Run regional validators against parsed data\n- `storage_lifecycle.py` — Check storage usage, apply retention policy\n\n**Adapter Layer:**\n- **REST:** FastAPI routes, middleware (auth, rate limit), dependency injection\n- **OCR:** PaddleOCR & EasyOCR adapters, HEIC/PDF preprocessor\n- **Repository:** PostgreSQL implementation with SQLAlchemy async\n- **Storage:** MinIO implementation\n- **Validators:** Region-specific validator modules, registry\n\n**Infrastructure Layer:**\n- **Config:** pydantic-settings for all env vars\n- **Database:** SQLAlchemy async engine, connection pool\n- **Queue:** PostgreSQL SKIP LOCKED implementation\n- **Scheduler:** APScheduler for storage lifecycle\n- **Logging:** structlog or standard logging with structured format\n\n**CLI:**\n- `admin.py` — API key create/list/revoke\n\n### 4. Data Model (DB Schema)\n\n```sql\n-- Core table\nCREATE TABLE documents (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n    type VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,           -- INVOICE, TICKET, PAYMENT_RECEIPT\n    region CHAR(2) NOT NULL,             -- ISO 3166-1 alpha-2\n    status VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL,         -- Enum values\n    media_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,     -- MIME type of original\n    image_key VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,     -- MinIO object key\n    original_filename VARCHAR(255),\n    parsed_data JSONB,                   -- Nullable, set after OCR\n    raw_text TEXT,                       -- Raw OCR output, nullable\n    confidence FLOAT,                    -- OCR confidence, nullable\n    validation_result JSONB,             -- Nullable, set after validation\n    error_detail JSONB,                  -- Error info if failed\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_documents_status ON documents(status);\nCREATE INDEX idx_documents_type ON documents(type);\nCREATE INDEX idx_documents_region ON documents(region);\nCREATE INDEX idx_documents_created_at ON documents(created_at DESC);\n\n-- API keys\nCREATE TABLE api_keys (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n    prefix VARCHAR(12) NOT NULL,         -- First 8 chars for display\n    key_hash VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL UNIQUE, -- SHA-256 hash\n    name VARCHAR(100),                   -- Human-readable label\n    revoked BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_api_keys_prefix ON api_keys(prefix);\nCREATE INDEX idx_api_keys_hash ON